          "guid": "mt5dkzpbuxnxgjyg",
          "message": {
            "text": "The live discriminator confirms a deterministic palette-cache identity defect without a tolerance. On macOS arm64 with Chromium 147.0.7727.15, the final DPR-1/2 run passed all 22 native source-color rows. Base2/base3 source PNG SHA-256 values were 91145b2c… and 83ac4321…; Domotion emitted two uses of only the first hash, and reversing DOM order duplicated only the other hash. Both records retained selectedRepresentation=colr, two SVG image uses, zero warnings, and no captured fontPalette fact. Focused unit/workflow tests passed 12/12 and the browser E2E passed 1/1.",
            "markdown": "The live discriminator confirms a deterministic palette-cache identity defect without a tolerance. On macOS arm64 with Chromium 147.0.7727.15, the final DPR-1/2 run passed all 22 native source-color rows. Base2/base3 source PNG SHA-256 values were 91145b2c… and 83ac4321…; Domotion emitted two uses of only the first hash, and reversing DOM order duplicated only the other hash. Both records retained selectedRepresentation=colr, two SVG image uses, zero warnings, and no captured fontPalette fact. Focused unit/workflow tests passed 12/12 and the browser E2E passed 1/1."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tests/font-palette-ownership-audit.e2e.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 5,
                  "endLine": 23,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "describe(\"DM-2350 live font-palette ownership discriminator\", () => {\n  it(\"proves source selection and the current palette-blind raster-cache signature\", async () => {\n    const report = await runFontPaletteOwnershipAudit({ dprs: [1] });\n    expect(report.verdict).toBe(\"confirmed-palette-identity-gap\");\n    expect(report.nativeRows).toHaveLength(FONT_PALETTE_CASES.length);\n    expect(report.nativeRows.every((row) => row.pass)).toBe(true);\n    expect(report.productionOrders).toHaveLength(2);\n    for (const row of report.productionOrders) {\n      expect(row.warnings).toEqual([]);\n      expect(row.sourcePngSha256[0]).not.toBe(row.sourcePngSha256[1]);\n      expect(row.capturedPngCount).toBe(2);\n      expect(row.capturedUniquePngCount).toBe(1);\n      expect(row.captureHasFontPaletteFact).toBe(false);\n      expect(row.selectedRepresentation).toBe(\"colr\");\n      expect(row.svgImageCount).toBe(2);\n    }\n    expect(report.productionOrders[0].capturedPngSha256[0])\n      .not.toBe(report.productionOrders[1].capturedPngSha256[0]);\n  }, 30_000);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
